WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:05.120
Okay, so this is the mark, right?

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:10.320
Is "Baby, It's Cold Outside" a date rape anthem?
Certain critics say "yes."

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:14.100
According to Snopes, the song
legitimizes sexual entrapment.

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:18.540
To avoid controversy, multiple
radio stations pulled it from holiday playlists.

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:24.580
For the record, the 74 year-old song is a
duet between a seemingly reluctant female

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:29.020
and a persistent suitor. It's old-fashioned
and that's part of its charm.

00:00:29.020 --> 00:00:32.520
To say that it's about rape
is nearly as absurd as claiming that it

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:36.660
sends the wrong message on global
warming. The song is about love and

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:41.420
mutual attraction. The two characters are
toying with one another — matching wits,

00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:48.000
having fun. Dropping the song has proved
to be a PR nightmare for radio stations.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:54.160
Many have deemed it an act of censorship.
A poll in Denver is typical: 95% of respondents

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:58.900
want it back on the air. So the stations are
now busy restoring this much-loved duet

00:00:58.900 --> 00:01:03.580
to the Christmas rotation, and several
versions of the song are surging in sales.

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:07.580
Civilization fought back and won.

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:13.380
What do you think about "Baby, It's Cold Outside"?
Should it be pulled from the airwaves?

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:17.940
Let us know in our poll. Also, let us know
what other topics you'd like our scholars

00:01:17.940 --> 00:01:22.170
to cover in 60 seconds and be
sure to LIKE and subscribe for more

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:26.450
research and videos from AEI.

